 "notes": "Single 22-way edge connector, rear view, drawn as one column of rows labelled with a letter and a number (A|1 ... Z|22, no G, I, O, Q). Each label is written once beside the row, so it is not stated whether it applies to the letter contact, the number contact or both; the number is recorded in 'pin', the letter in 'also'. The drawing names no connector, so it is called P1. Rows D|4 to R|14, U|17 and V|18 are drawn blank (skipped). INPUT bracket covers A|1 (+) and B|2 (-); OUT bracket covers S|15 (+) and T|16 (-). Original Ward-Beck Systems Ltd. sheet (manual page, file name 'P6'): DRN. DM, DATE OCT 74, size A, ISS. 1; MAT'L and FINISH struck out. Read independently from this picture; it shows the same 462-04-004 sheet as the M462 copy."
